This is a good point. I checked the memory required to run PC-Nethack
and its somewhere around 300K. How about overlaying a little less of the
code. It seems that almost every time something new happens (like walking
over objects, running into your dog, monsters entering the room, 
fighting, ...) there is a disk access. Some of the more frequently used
code (like walking over objects) could be moved out of the overlay. 
There seems to be plenty of space to work with.

